# Build-context exclusions for docker/dsh/Dockerfile* (context = repo root).
#
# node_modules MUST NOT enter the context: the tree carries host-platform
# binaries (linux-x64 / darwin / win32 esbuild, sharp, node-pty, ripgrep), and
# copying them into an image for a different CPU leaves `pnpm install` to
# reconcile a tree of unloadable native modules. The image installs from the
# lockfile instead, which resolves the optional dependencies for its own
# platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# .git is intentionally kept in the build context: the dev image ships
# /app/.git so a developer can `git pull` / `git diff` inside the running dev
# container (dsh-dev.gb10). client-build-environment.ts still prefers the
# DSH_CLIENT_COMMIT_HASH build-arg, so carrying .git does not change build output.

# Build outputs are produced inside the image by `pnpm run build`.
**/lib
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state that must never be baked into an image. Only a repository-root
# .dsh is developer state; `**/.dsh` would also drop the tracked
# examples/acp-agent snapshot fixtures that live under a .dsh directory.
.env
.env.*
/.dsh
coverage
